 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? About one liter per hour is a good rule of thumb. Are you drinking enough in the first place? Then have small bottle at each stop, and plan to top it up at the half point. If you' out for more than two hours, yes. A bar or two will keep you going until the next stop. You can get away with it on a short ride, but as the distance grows, so does the risk. A bar or two in tank is cheap insurance.",
